meta {
  name: Register Device
  type: http
  seq: 80
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/devices/register?code={{functionKey}}
  body: json
  auth: none
}

body:json {
  {
    "platform": "windows",
    "pushToken": "your-push-notification-token-here"
  }
}

docs {
  # Register Device
  
  Registers a device for push notifications.
  
  ## Authentication
  Requires a valid JWT token in the Authorization header (Bearer token).
  
  ## Request Body
  - `platform` (required): Device platform ("windows", "ios", "android")
  - `pushToken` (required): The push notification token from the device
  
  ## Response Fields
  - `message`: Confirmation message
  - `deviceId` (guid): The registered device ID
  
  ## Behavior
  - If a device with the same platform is already registered for this user, the token is updated
  - Tokens are used to send push notifications for rating reminders and other alerts
  
  ## Error Responses
  - `400 Bad Request`: Missing platform or pushToken
  - `401 Unauthorized`: Invalid or missing authentication token
  - `404 Not Found`: User not registered
}
